From 50ab8ce7c6b52f4656361a9d63d3e9cd526387cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@buttzeppelin>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:12:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Zeppelin F-223: ZepModernM2 external skeletons (SKID)

- the .skel (FileDataPaths, else <model stem>.skel) has SKS1/SKB1/SKA1 spliced into the
  body; every track array rebased (inline keys to the body, streamed ones left to the .anim)
- skeleton .anim files: AFM2 slides down as before, the sequence's bone (AFSB) and
  attachment (AFSA) inner arrays are rebased onto those chunks before relocation
- a parent skeleton's (SKPD) streamed animations are not loaded (parent bone layout)
Verified: retail bloodtick (3149134 skel, 104 bones) renders and animates.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ByrZ7GxoHC9wfGdkRwtqCX
---
